{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350562-is-non-lethal-op-or-am-i-doing-it-wrong","id":1350562,"title":"Is non-lethal OP, or am I doing it wrong?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-23T18:33:01-08:00","id":1350562,"title":"Is non-lethal OP, or am I doing it wrong?","content":"The non-lethal weapon tag as written, seems unclear on how it works<br /> Because you &quot;assign successes&quot; rather than inflict damage, it seems like even a single success on the attack roll will stun the target (as their base defense is covered by the base 1 enhancement for the weapon)<br /> The now stunned target, can attempt to &quot;shake off&quot; the effects as an action, but they're already stunned, and have a difficulty to the &quot;shake off&quot; roll? meanwhile, the attacker just stands there and blasts them each round until they fall over?<br /> It's really confusing since the weapon tag &quot;stun&quot; and the status effect &quot;stunned&quot; operate very differently.<br /> <br /> Further, it is unclear if sonics are covered by perikinesis 2, as it wouldn't be affected by an armor rating, and sonic attacks don't have the &quot;continuous&quot; tag. Adaptation also only allows defense against environmental damage with the &quot;continuous&quot; tag, and makes no mention of sonics. Iatrosis seems to possibly be able to help mitigate the effects after the fact, but I don't see any &quot;defense&quot; against it in the books.<br /> <br /> Also, sonic blades make no sense: They have the sonic tag, which means they ignore all armor that isn't &quot;Environmental 1/2&quot; but they also have the non-penetrating tag which means &quot;Doubles the value of all soft armor&quot; so, 0 X 2 = 0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T20:29:29-08:00","id":1350574,"title":"","content":"Stunned is really confusing. It has a Complication that prevents you from doing anything, but Complications aren't supposed to affect success or failure, so how does that work, exactly?<br /> <br /> Anyway, my best guess at how Non-Lethal is supposed to work is that it contributes successes to Stunned's Complication level. When someone takes an action, they have to first spend successes to overcome the Complication (and thus end the Condition) and then they can spend any extra successes on the action. Alternatively, they can just spend their whole round doing the &quot;shake it off&quot; action. But the language of Stunned as a Complication means that even though it says you can't do anything, you clearly can or else the Complication would be meaningless.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of errors in some of the sample equipment. Sonic Blade might be an example, but that _could_ be read as &quot;Sonic Blade doubles the Soft Armor value of all Environmental armor but ignores non-Environmental armor.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T03:27:24-08:00","id":1350619,"title":"","content":"The non-lethal tag states that you can either act with the complication, or spend an action shaking it off.<br /> The big question is, does the complication affect the &quot;shake it off&quot; roll?<br /> <br /> And if that's how we read sonic blades, shouldn't all sonic weapons have the non-pen tag?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T04:48:12-08:00","id":1350621,"title":"","content":"The shake-off is to remove successes before they are unconscious... not for stunned... so you either stun them or you try to make them unconscious.<br /> <br /> And for sonic blades, yep... if the armour doesn\u2019t have environmental then it bypasses it all.<br /> If the armour does have environmental, then good luck getting through the soft armor defence.<br /> <br /> Based on page 125, in core for the stun tag, it notes that stun is purchased with the inflict damage stunt but instead gives a +2 complication.<br /> (So soft armor does apply for stun if the armor has the right tags)<br /> <br /> Though this is a bit of joining the dots, I\u2019m assuming that non-lethal is an upgrade to the stun tag as it allows them to either stun or knock unconscious, rather than re-writing how stun works for other weapons.<br /> <br /> (Also, just an opinion based on jumping around between various books for the last hour <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23598-quilligoth","name":"quilligoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T06:04:36-08:00","id":1350628,"title":"","content":"Quilligoth is right as far as I can understand. The stub tag is different form the non-letal. Stun in simpler and not cumulative (at least as I understand), and the condition end automatically according to the source, like an stun gun. The Non-lethal requires more bookkeeping and can be worn off by the target, like an impact in the head or something like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T06:38:18-08:00","id":1350635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quilligoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350562-is-non-lethal-op-or-am-i-doing-it-wrong?p=1350621#post1350621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shake-off is to remove successes before they are unconscious... not for stunned... so you either stun them or you try to make them unconscious.<br /> <br /> (Also, just an opinion based on jumping around between various books for the last hour <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This attack normally produces the Stunned Status Condition but if the attacker allocates at least four successes to the attack, the target gains the Unconscious Status Condition&quot;<br /> It certainly reads that it stuns you if you don't have enough successes to render the target unconscious right away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T06:40:43-08:00","id":1350636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350562-is-non-lethal-op-or-am-i-doing-it-wrong?p=1350628#post1350628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quilligoth is right as far as I can understand. The stub tag is different form the non-letal. Stun in simpler and not cumulative (at least as I understand), and the condition end automatically according to the source, like an stun gun. The Non-lethal requires more bookkeeping and can be worn off by the target, like an impact in the head or something like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the stun tag, and the non-lethal tag allow the target to shake off the effects.<br /> Per the status condition Stunned on core p 108<br /> &quot;A character can overcome the Complication associated with the damage source (see \u201cIndirect Damage,\u201d below) to end the Condition early.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's this crossing back and forth between &quot;attack&quot; and &quot;Indirect damage&quot; that I think is the core of the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T02:39:01-08:00","id":1350787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baladain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350562-is-non-lethal-op-or-am-i-doing-it-wrong?p=1350635#post1350635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;This attack normally produces the Stunned Status Condition but if the attacker allocates at least four successes to the attack, the target gains the Unconscious Status Condition&quot;<br /> It certainly reads that it stuns you if you don't have enough successes to render the target unconscious right away.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording for the unconscious says you can allocate successes and can also accumulate successes over multiple attacks and if you achieve 4 before they are thrown off, then the target is unconscious.<br /> <br /> I read that as accumulating successes towards unconscious specifically (only...). Not that you can multiple purpose them.<br /> <br /> And to add another wrinkle you could use a success(es) for Stun per normal and allocate additional successes towards unconscious.<br /> Which I feel l brings it inline with standard injury and critical stunts.<br /> <br /> And yeah the crossing over between attack and indirect damage makes the whole thing a bit difficult work out what it is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23598-quilligoth","user":"quilligoth","date":". 11-25-2019, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23598-quilligoth","name":"quilligoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T03:40:27-08:00","id":1350789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quilligoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350562-is-non-lethal-op-or-am-i-doing-it-wrong?p=1350787#post1350787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to add another wrinkle you could use a success(es) for Stun per normal and allocate additional successes towards unconscious.<br /> Which I feel l brings it inline with standard injury and critical stunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, this is consistent with the intent. Non-lethal Tag weapons work broadly the same as lethal weapons, but you don\u2019t purchase \u2018Inflict Damage\u2019 and impart an Injury Condition, you choose \u2018Inflict Stunned\u2019 and the Stunned status condition. You don\u2019t choose \u2018Critical\u2019 with your four extra successes, you choose \u2018Unconscious\u2019 with them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, run it as per normal combat, but with the additional considerations that you can accumulate the four \u2018Unconscious\u2019 successes over multiple turns, and the target can try shaking them off over multiple turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T12:29:15-08:00","id":1351092,"title":"","content":"I have to believe that Stunned is very difficult to manage and balance across many game systems including but limited to D&amp;D, Exalted, CoD, CoD a d Storypath. Seems to rank right up there with stealth and grapple.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T04:32:36-08:00","id":1351627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350562-is-non-lethal-op-or-am-i-doing-it-wrong?p=1350789#post1350789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, this is consistent with the intent. Non-lethal Tag weapons work broadly the same as lethal weapons, but you don\u2019t purchase \u2018Inflict Damage\u2019 and impart an Injury Condition, you choose \u2018Inflict Stunned\u2019 and the Stunned status condition. You don\u2019t choose \u2018Critical\u2019 with your four extra successes, you choose \u2018Unconscious\u2019 with them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, run it as per normal combat, but with the additional considerations that you can accumulate the four \u2018Unconscious\u2019 successes over multiple turns, and the target can try shaking them off over multiple turns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That actually simplifies things quite a bit, thank you.<br /> The one major question that remains, however, is: Does the complication from being stunned apply to rolls to shake off stun/almost unconscious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T15:43:46-08:00","id":1351728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baladain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350562-is-non-lethal-op-or-am-i-doing-it-wrong?p=1351627#post1351627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That actually simplifies things quite a bit, thank you.<br /> The one major question that remains, however, is: Does the complication from being stunned apply to rolls to shake off stun/almost unconscious</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could if you wanted to, for a more Iron-Age game, but I'd frankly find it tiresome to keep track of. I'd let the shake-off rolls be normal; if the PC is good at shaking things off, they were probably built that way, and your NPCs need a different way to take them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}